Foundation readiness: demonstrate the abilities already learned (@greek-scholarly-foundation: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-scholarly-path, #philosophy @greek-philological-study, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-philological-study) { r_2P555101Z0VGGZ14M12HRWKSYY
Use the [foundation survey](../Ancient-Greek-Philosophy.lingua#r_464ZHR7ZYC234A0XX2QEW47VB3), the [first argument review](../socratic/Argument-review.lingua#r_3879MMB9TCFTCMJ2SPYG32ZDS0), and the [comparative investigation](../questions/Comparative-investigation.lingua#r_20BK69Q76HJXAGZ5J1T097X29G) as evidence for this stage.

Show that you can locate and explain a primary question and argument in each major part: earlier Greek thought; Socratic inquiry; Plato; Aristotle's methods, nature, ethics, politics, and art; the Hellenistic schools; and later Platonism. Place authors, genres, and transmitting sources in their relevant settings without turning chronology into a theory of inevitable progress.

Reconstruct arguments from passages rather than only reporting a doctrine. Compare a serious objection with a response. Distinguish an author's text, a dramatic speaker, an ancient report, a translation, and a later commentary.

**Required work:** keep a portfolio of located reconstructions and one developed comparison. Read the complete short Socratic dialogues supporting that comparison; for longer treatises, record the books and argument sequences studied and explain their role in the work.

**Readiness check:** another reader can locate the evidence and recognise the positions you reconstruct. You can explain which premise an objection challenges and identify where further history, language, logic, or textual work is needed.

If the difficulty is local, return to the relevant [shared preparation](../foundations/Reading-tools.lingua#r_5DTAXMW53NH7ABW23PMFSSBQEF). Evidence already produced through another route can satisfy an ability here if its meaning and depth match.

Completing this portfolio establishes foundation readiness. Continue with [textual study](Philological-study.lingua#r_353E4E4WH3BWFHHJNZMPKBPEXF) and [scholarly inquiry](Scholarly-inquiry.lingua#r_2FEBDJ8R5JDHXX54TSATY2CRVZ); full study completion uses the [later requirements](Research-completion.lingua#r_41G7P2Y9HYXMVAF53MV2QYT1CD).
